# Rover 75 (saloon), 1999-2005.
#
# The Rover 75 was the last Rover designed before the BMW sale and the last car of
# the Rover line: launched in 1999, it replaced the 800 and carried the marque until
# MG Rover collapsed in 2005. It is the most rounded and most chrome-detailed of the
# Rover family in the pakset.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_75
#
# Dimensions 4.747 x 1.778 x 1.424 m, wheelbase 2.746 m; the published saloon
# figures. The estate (4.791 m) and the limousine were not modelled.
#
# Colours: Copperleaf Red, Starlight Silver, White Gold and Wedgwood Blue, all Rover
# UK offerings of the launch period. DVSA first-registration shares for 1999-2005
# are measured, so no era adjustment is needed: red 4, silver 4, white 3, blue 3.
# Total 14. Provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 190 km/h, at the Rover 25's tier: the 75's volume engines were the 1.8 and
# 2.0 K-series and the 2.5 KV6, and the pakset figure is a game-balance value rather
# than the model's maximum. Comfort 105/488, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 105, one step
# below the Corsa E's 105/488 tier and at the top of the private-car comfort range
# for its date. Classes 1,2: the 75 was a genuine executive car, not a repmobile.
#
# Dates are road presence: June 1999 intro, retires staggered 2010-2015 on an
# eleven- to sixteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-75.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/rover-75.dae (80 objects). References:
# citycars/references/rover-75/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0).
#
# Accepted low-poly deviations, recorded rather than corrected: the model is more
# angular than the photographed compound curves, and the Gate B camera angles are
# approximate and orthographic rather than calibrated.

obj=citycar
name=Rover75(CopperleafRed)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=4
intro_year=1999
intro_month=6
retire_year=2012
retire_month=6
speed=190
length=3
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=105
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=488

